It seems like you must have an older version of NMAKE.  Mine works fine
as Timo layed it out for NMAKE.  What you should do is look for the
CMD makefile variable.  There will be a couple of them, all but one
will be commented out.  Sounds like you need the one set to CMD /c,
not the empty string.  The section designed to handle dmake will have
the correct definition of CMD for you...

